message:
span-to improvements: magnet snap enabler

With zero additional compute cost, the `snapPick` function will now return both:

- the regular `worldPos`, as in standard surface picking; this picking has high precision
- the `snappedWorldPos`, will be `null` if snap didn't happen, or the world coordinate if it spanned

This enables a new kind of logic in the `snapPick` consuming side:

```js
const pickResult = snapPick (canvasCoords, 15 /*radius*/, "vertex");

if (pickResult) {
    if (pickResult.snappedWorldPos) {
        // the picker snapped to vertex/edge
    } else {
        // regular surface pick; pickResult.worldPos will be set
    }
}
```

Expose the `snapPick` method through the `Scene` class

So we can do;

```js
snaPickResult = scene.snapPick({
    canvasPos: [ 45, 12 ],
    snapRadius: 15,
    snapType: "vertex" | "edge",
});
```
